      "markdown": "# ESP32-S3 Neural Stream Bandwidth Experiment Report\n\nGenerated at: `2026-08-26T09:00:25.565230+00:00`\n\n## Experiment Context\n\nThis report summarizes an ESP32-S3 WiFi/UDP stream used as a neural-data surrogate for downstream spike-sorting and compression experiments. The main engineering question is how much packetized throughput the wireless link can sustain while keeping sequence-gap loss, CRC errors, jitter, and end-to-end latency within an acceptable range.\n\n## Key Results\n\n| Metric | Value |\n| --- | ---: |\n| Time filter | all data |\n| Capture start UTC | 2026-08-26T08:55:20.172041+00:00 |\n| Capture end UTC | 2026-08-26T08:57:40.692898+00:00 |\n| Captured frames | 110086 |\n| Capture duration | 140.52 s |\n| Transport | udp |\n| Payload bytes | 1472 |\n| Frame bytes | 1486 |\n| Target FPS | 1000 |\n| Target throughput | 1451.17 KiB/s |\n| Mean FPS | 1068.32 |\n| FPS range | 0.21 - 3487.80 |\n| Mean throughput | 1550.32 KiB/s |\n| Throughput range | 0.30 - 5061.40 KiB/s |\n| Total missing frames by sequence | 140317 |\n| Missing frames by in-window gaps | 140434 |\n| Longest consecutive missing run | 1425 |\n| Window missing-frame sum | 74189 |\n| Mean loss rate | 15.9158% |\n| Max loss rate | 57.8260% |\n| CRC/resync errors | 0 |\n| Old/duplicate frames | 1575 |\n| Mean arrival jitter | 228.919 ms |\n| Max arrival jitter | 6470.392 ms |\n| Mean bandwidth volatility | 1123.925 KiB/s |\n| Max bandwidth volatility | 2102.000 KiB/s |\n| Latency samples | 110083 |\n| Mean latency | 2598.590 ms |\n| P50 latency | 2221.795 ms |\n| P95 latency | 2363.586 ms |\n| P99 latency | 16279.208 ms |\n| Relative latency samples | 110086 |\n| Mean relative latency | 375.820 ms |\n| P50 relative latency | -2.542 ms |\n| P95 relative latency | 139.284 ms |\n| P99 relative latency | 14055.062 ms |\n\n## Quality Gates\n\n| Gate | Status | Value | Criterion |\n| --- | --- | ---: | --- |\n| CRC / parser integrity | PASS | 0 | crc_errors == 0 |\n| Application loss | WARN | 57.8260% | max loss <= 0.1% |\n| Mean frame rate | PASS | 1068.32 | mean fps >= 95% target |\n| Mean throughput | PASS | 1550.32 KiB/s | mean throughput >= 95% target |\n| Latency availability | PASS | 110083 | Latency samples present |\n\n## Figures\n\n![Bandwidth Timeseries 20260826 170025](figures/bandwidth_timeseries_20260826_170025.png)\n\n![Latency Histogram 20260826 170025](figures/latency_histogram_20260826_170025.png)\n\n\n## Interpretation Notes\n\n- A healthy UDP run should keep loss rate and CRC/resync errors at zero for the current 1000 fps x 1472 byte workload.\n- Arrival jitter captures UDP datagram cadence variability; sequence gaps represent application-visible packet loss rather than TCP backpressure.\n- Absolute latency is only trustworthy when both the ESP32-S3 clock and the laptop clock are synchronized.\n- Relative latency from the first packet is useful even when the laptop clock is not synchronized, because it removes the fixed clock offset and still shows queue buildup.\n- If absolute latency looks suspiciously large, prefer the relative-latency panel and repeat the run with working NTP before drawing one-way latency conclusions.\n- Treat the quality gates as screening checks. A WARN does not automatically invalidate the run, but it should be explained in the experiment notes.\n\n## Experiment Manifest\n\n```json\n{\n  \"experiment_id\": \"udp-s3-dynamic-tx-1472-saturated-goodput-sqp-on-hat-left-posterior-1m-rep1-20260826_165503\",\n  \"condition_label\": \"s3-dynamic-tx-1472-saturated-goodput-sqp-on-hat-left-posterior-1m-rep1\",\n  \"operator\": \"\",\n  \"started_at_local\": \"\",\n  \"transport\": \"udp\",\n  \"target_fps\": 1000,\n  \"application_context\": {\n    \"downstream_task\": \"UDP maximum-throughput search for neural stream transport\",\n    \"notes\": \"The ESP32-S3 sender disables FPS pacing and sends numbered 1472-byte UDP datagrams as fast as the socket path allows. The current high-throughput diagnostic profile uses static payload bytes and disables CRC so it can be compared against the official ESP-IDF iperf UDP TX baseline.\",\n    \"workload\": \"spike_stream_surrogate\"\n  },\n  \"network\": {\n    \"hotspot_device\": \"Windows laptop mobile hotspot\",\n    \"receiver_ip\": \"192.168.137.1\",\n    \"receiver_port\": 5001,\n    \"ssid\": \"Dennis\"\n  },\n  \"stream\": {\n    \"frame_bytes\": 1486,\n    \"nominal_rate_kib_s\": 1451.171875,\n    \"pacing\": \"configured\",\n    \"payload_bytes\": 1472,\n    \"target_fps\": 1000,\n    \"transport\": \"WiFi + UDP\"\n  },\n  \"condition\": {\n    \"duration_min\": 2,\n    \"purpose\": \"unpaced UDP maximum-throughput measurement with per-packet sequence logging\"\n  },\n  \"frame_bytes\": 1486,\n  \"operator_notes\": \"Hardware: ESP32-S3; Power: power bank; Placement: on-hat left posterior; Distance: 1 m; Duration: 5 min; Note: formal detached field trace, reset during receiver arming window, sequence-aware source-port handling\",\n  \"payload_bytes\": 1472,\n  \"receiver_started_at_local\": \"2026-08-26T16:55:03\",\n  \"udp_socket_rcvbuf\": 4194304\n}\n```\n",
